  "raw": "ima Vavi\nIn its draft manifesto, Cosatu has called for the \"expropriation of land without compensation, a redistribution of land to the people and landless people in particular, the immediate expropriation and redistribution of land to the black majority population and the nationalisation of all mines, mines and coal mines\".\nThe call for expropriation has resonated with labour activists and the public at large. This is despite the fact there is no legislation in place to facilitate such actions.\n\"We have no constitution in place, no laws and procedures have been put in place. We have not been given a timeline as to implementation,\" said Cosatu secretary-general, Zwelinzima Vavi.\n\"We don't have the constitutional framework, so how does expropriation happen? What is the timing for that? Expropriation of land without compensation for one day in particular? How does the land acquisition process happen without the necessary mechanisms? These are the",
